module Core

### Represents the protocol for modulo-width multiplication.
### `WrappingMultiplicable` is for bounded bit-width types whose multiplication
### result discards overflow bits instead of trapping.
protocol WrappingMultiplicable
  ### Returns the wrapping product of this value and `you`.
  ### The result preserves only the low bits that fit in the conforming type.
  ### :param you: The other factor.
  ### :returns: The resulting `Me` value.
  @readonly
  routine Me.mul_wrap(you: Me) -> Me
